ineffably:
There was an evening when the sky was clear,
Ineffably translucent in its blue;
The tide was falling and the sea withdrew

inescapably:
Of hens, the wheeze of a pump, she needs must hear;
She inescapably must endure to feel
Across her teeth the grinding of a backing wagon

inebriates:
She banged on the table and broke the plates;
She jeered at the passing inebriates;
And tore all her dresses and ripped her socks;
